hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"243","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a slave woman or a man used to clean the mosque. When the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, did not find him, he inquired about him. They said: He has passed away. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Why did you not inform me about him?"" They replied, and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Show me his grave."" So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, came to his grave and offered his funeral prayer."
"244","Abbad bin Mansur said: I heard Abu al-Mahzam narrate: I stayed with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) for ten years, I heard him narrate, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever attends a funeral and lifts it three times has fulfilled the right of that (funeral) which was due upon him."""
"245","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever participated in a funeral and lifted it three times, he has fulfilled the right that was due upon him.”"
"246","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a funeral procession. When I walked, he would go ahead of me, and then I started walking faster. When I walked faster, I went ahead of him. There was a man beside me, he said: The earth is being folded for you."
"247","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw the grave of his noble mother, so he wept and made those around him weep as well. Then he said: ""I sought permission from my Lord to visit the grave of my noble mother, and He granted me permission. And I sought permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not grant me permission. So visit (the graves), for they remind you of the Hereafter."""
"248","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith similar to the previous one."
"249","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever attends a funeral and returns before the burial, for him is one qirat, and if he stays with it until the burial, for him are two qirats. The smallest of them (qirat) is like the mountain of Uhud."""
"250","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever offers the funeral prayer will have one qirat of reward, and whoever remains with it until the burial will have two qirats of reward, and the smallest of these two is like the mountain of Uhud."""
"251","Jallas narrates: Marwan bin Hakam passed by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was narrating hadith, so he said: ""Abu Hurairah! Divide your speech, make the hadith into parts."" He replied: ""Marwan! Leave us to ourselves."" The narrator stated, then he (Marwan) returned and said to him: ""How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicating in the funeral prayer?"" He replied: ""What I have said, do you count it?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""He used to supplicate: 'O Allah! You created him, You took his soul, You guided him to Islam, You know his outward and inward, we have come as intercessors, so forgive him.'"""
"252","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the funeral prayer, he used to supplicate: ""O Allah! You created him, You guided him towards Islam, You took his soul, You are aware of his hidden and open states, we have come to You as intercessors for him, so forgive him."""
"253","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in a marfu’ form that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, he (the deceased) hears the sound of their sandals, their movement, when they turn away from him.”"
"254","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man passed away and his good qualities were mentioned, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Then another man passed away and his bad qualities were mentioned, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Some people were surprised at this and asked: O Messenger of Allah! What has become obligatory? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are witnesses over one another."""
"255","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever passes away and his two close neighbors testify regarding him, saying: O Allah! We know only good about him, then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to the angels: I make you witnesses that I have forgiven My servant because of the testimony of these two men, and I have pardoned him for the things about which they do not know."""
"256","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever sends peace upon me, Allah returns my soul to me so that I may reply to his greeting."""
"257","Yazid bin Aws narrated: When Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill, his wife began to weep over him. He said to her: Have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said? She replied: Of course. Then when he passed away, Yazid said: I met that honorable lady and asked her: What did Abu Musa say to you? Did you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said? She replied: Of course. Then she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wails (in mourning), shaves her head, or tears her clothes is not from among us."""
"258","Qartha’ narrated: When Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill, his wife began to wail. Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said to her: “Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said?” She replied: “Why not?” So she became silent. Later, she was asked, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the one who wails (in mourning), shaves the head (in grief), and tears the clothes.”"
"259","Lady Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We were in the house of Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If two Muslims (husband and wife) have three children who die before reaching the age of puberty, they will be brought and stopped at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to them: Enter Paradise. They will say: How can we enter while our parents have not entered? Then it will be said to them: I do not know, the second or third time, enter Paradise and your parents as well. Thus, this is the statement of Allah the Exalted: The intercession of intercessors will not benefit them."""
"260","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were washing his daughter, so he said: “Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you feel it is necessary, and in the last washing add camphor or a little camphor to the water. And when you have finished, inform me.” So when we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper towards us and said: “Wrap her body with it.”"
"261","Sayyida Hafsa bint Sirin (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begin from her right side and from the parts of ablution (when giving the ritual bath)."" And Sayyida Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: ""I made her hair into three braids."""
"262","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We made three braids of the hair of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then we gathered all of them together and placed them behind her."
"263","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: One of the daughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) told us: “Wash her with water and lotus leaves an odd number of times, three times or five times, or more if you feel it necessary, and in the last washing add camphor or a little camphor to the water. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) threw his waist-wrapper towards us and said: “Wrap her body with it.”"
"264","Hisham narrated similarly with the same chain of transmission."
"265","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Among the things we were pledged upon was that we would not wail (over the dead). Only five women among us fulfilled this: Umm Sulaym, the wife of Mu‘adh bin Abi Sabrah (may Allah be pleased with him), or the wife of Mu‘adh (may Allah be pleased with him), the daughter of Abu Sabrah, and another woman. And she was not prepared for it until the day of Harrah, when the women participated in it until she stood up; they would not prepare themselves for it."
"266","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: When this verse was revealed: ""When believing women come to you to pledge that they will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery... and will not disobey you in what is right,"" she (Umm Atiyyah) said: Lamentation (wailing) was also included in this. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Except for the women of such-and-such tribe, for they helped me in the days of ignorance, so it is necessary for me to help them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Except for the women of such-and-such tribe."""
"267","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took a pledge from us, and in it was that we would not wail (over the dead). Only five of us fulfilled it, and Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) was among them."
"268","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We were forbidden from following funeral processions, but we were not strictly forbidden."
"269","Hisham narrated from this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"270","Sayyida Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We (women) were forbidden from following funeral processions, but it was not an emphatic prohibition."
"271","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to teach him this supplication just as he used to teach him a surah of the Qur'an: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah (Dajjal), and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death."""
"272","Abu Ma'bad narrated: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) led the funeral prayer, then said Allahu Akbar, then recited Surah Al-Fatihah and recited it aloud, then after that said three takbirs, and said: I recited aloud so that you may know that this is the Sunnah."
"273","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: There was retribution (qisas) among the Children of Israel, but there was no blood money (diyah) among them. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said for this Ummah: ""Prescribed for you is retribution in the case of murder: the free for the free..."" until the verse reached: ""But if any remission is made by his brother..."" The narrator stated: His forgiving means his accepting blood money. Thus, following and demanding it in a good manner is prescribed. He said: He will demand it from him in a good manner and will enjoin kindness upon him. This addition is narrated from Sufyan: ""This is a concession and mercy from your Lord."" What is meant is: accepting blood money for intentional murder."
